close_reason: "Delivered the persistent derived mutation-event projection, stable cursors, bounded filtering, SDK async subscription, SDK-backed NDJSON CLI, contracts/docs, installed-package proof, and exact 100% coverage."
body: "## Context\nExtension hooks (registerHook) fire only in-process during a mutation. Cross-process, the only way another agent learns about workspace changes is polling (pm context / pm list), which at thousands of concurrent agents is both token-expensive and racy. The pm-slack package (lifecycle notifications) exists as prior art for the *consumer* side but has no first-class producer primitive to build on.\n\n## Proposal\nA read-only mutation event stream derived from the append-only history streams (no new write path, no daemon — consistent with ADR pm-i7i4):\n1. CLI: `pm events --follow [--since <cursor>] [--type ...] [--author ...] [--item ...]` emitting one JSON object per line (NDJSON, per the pm-646c convention) so it composes with grep/jq/xargs (pm-m9xv story, pm-psy1 scripting contract).\n2. SDK: a subscription/iterator primitive (async iterable over history events with a durable cursor) — the layer packages like pm-slack, pm-web, and future coordination tooling rebuild on.\n3. Cursor semantics: stable resumable position (per-stream offsets or global logical clock) so an agent can disconnect and catch up without replaying everything; must stay O(new events) at 100k-1M items, which couples this to the pm-9rxu read-index work.\n\n## Non-goals\n- No long-running server/daemon requirement: --follow is an optional convenience over poll-with-cursor; single-shot `pm events --since <cursor>` must work for stateless agents.\n- Not a message bus: events are facts about mutations already committed to history, never commands.\n\n## Relationships\n- Parent pm-dj98 (multi-agent safety): reduces polling contention and enables claim/handoff coordination patterns.\n- pm-646c (NDJSON), pm-psy1 (scripting contract), pm-9rxu/pm-801d (index makes tailing cheap), pm-usfg (SDK primitive first, CLI shim second), pm-slack package (first consumer to migrate).\n- Horizon: mid-to-long — after NDJSON output mode and the persistent read index land.\n\n## Duplicate check (2026-07-07 review #16)\nSearched \"watch mode event subscription\", \"watch follow tail stream\", \"pm watch subscribe mutations\", \"notification agent coordination\" — no existing item covers a cross-process event/subscription primitive; nearest matches were in-process hook work and the pm-slack package (consumer only)."
